.TH CERT\-VIEWER 1 "November 2026" "cert\-viewer" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cert\-viewer \- view and inspect multiple x509 certificates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cert\-viewer
.RI [ flags ]
.IR file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cert\-viewer
reads x509 certificates from one or more files, verifies them against each
other and the system root certificates, and shows them sorted by their
certificate chains.
.PP
A file can contain multiple PEM encoded certificates or a single DER encoded
certificate. Other PEM blocks, like private keys, are ignored, as are
directories. A certificate found in more than one file or block is shown once
with all its sources.
.PP
Each chain is shown from the leaf certificate up to its root, indented by its
depth. Self signed CA certificates from the given files are trusted like
system root certificates. Certificates which could not be verified are shown
last, together with the reason.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help message.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-disablesysroot
Do not use the system root certificates for the verification.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Print the certificates as JSON.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, also if certificates could not be verified.
.TP
.B 1
A file could not be read or parsed, no certificate was found, or no file was
given.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line flags.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show a certificate together with its chain:
.PP
.RS
.B cert\-viewer server.crt chain.pem
.RE
.PP
Show the expiry date of all certificates of a file, using
.BR jq (1):
.PP
.RS
.nf
.B cert\-viewer \-\-json fullchain.pem | \e
.B "  jq \-r \(aq.[] | [.validity.not_after, .subject.common_name] | @tsv\(aq"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openssl\-x509 (1)
.PP
.nh
https://github.com/mgit\-at/cert\-viewer
